# ...but deploy/cloudflare-explorer/build/ is SOURCE, not a build artifact:
# it holds the scripts that produce and ship the hosted explorer
# (precompute.py, upload.sh, reshard.py, verify-all.sh, bundle-duckdb.sh).
# The generic build/ rule above was silently swallowing all of them, leaving
# the deployment unreproducible from a clean checkout. Negating the directory
# itself is required -- git will not descend into an excluded directory, so
# re-including only its contents would not work.
!deploy/cloudflare-explorer/build/
# Generated by bindings/atlas/3.1/tools/build_fixtures.py: 8,339 files / 73 MB
# of conformance cases that no review ever read, and that any generator edit
# rewrote wholesale. What git carries instead is the two artifacts that state
# the contract -- fixtures/corpus.json (a sealed bundle member) and
# fixtures-receipt.json (the digest the rebuild must reproduce). `make
# check-generated` rebuilds the tree in ~9s on a cold checkout and fails if it
# does not match the receipt.
bindings/atlas/3.1/fixtures/valid/
bindings/atlas/3.1/fixtures/invalid/
bindings/atlas/3.1/.atlas-3.1-fixtures.tmp/
.playwright-cli/
.playwright-mcp/
test-results/
.env
.claude/worktrees/
.wrangler/
# Generated by the external doc generator (wiki/metadata.json records version
# 1.0.1 at commit d62bc1cc): a 14,161,039-byte dependency graph keyed by
# `path::symbol` that embeds the source code it describes, so it duplicates
# the tree, goes stale on the next commit, and is recreated by re-running the
# generator. Untracked here to match SpicySearch, which already ignores it.
wiki/temp/
